{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_1_frobenius","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_1_frobenius","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_1_frobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_1_frobenius","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_1_frobenius.lean#L36-L51","doc":"**Axiom 1 — Haar-state Frobenius pairing** (pattern C — named,\nnot asserted).\n\n**Lemma statement** (from manuscript): the Haar state\n$h = \\int_{A}$ on $A = \\mathcal{O}_{q}(G)$ is faithful; equivalently,\nthe pairing $(a, b) \\mapsto h(ab)$ is non-degenerate and induces an\nisomorphism $A \\xrightarrow{\\sim} A^{\\vee}$, verifying axiom~(1) of\n[quantum observable universe](#def:quantum-observable-universe).\n\nWe **name** non-degeneracy as the bijectivity of the induced pairing\nmap — a `Prop` over the context's primitive data — rather than\nprojecting it from self-assuming `pairing_inj`/`pairing_surj` fields.\nAn instance of this proposition is the open faithfulness claim. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:qou-exists-axiom-1","label":"lem:qou-exists-axiom-1","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-exists-axiom-1.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.pairing_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.pairing_map","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_1_frobenius.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Frobenius pairing `(a, b) ↦ h(a · b)` induced map `A → A^∨`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.h","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_1_frobenius.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Haar state `h : A → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.A_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.A_dual","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_1_frobenius.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Dual object `A^∨`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.A","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_1_frobenius.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Hopf algebra carrier `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_1_frobenius.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom1FrobeniusContext","kind":"class","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_1_frobenius.lean#L19-L34","doc":"Carrier for the `exists_axiom_1_frobenius` data — only the\nprimitive, non-conclusory fields (pattern C): the Hopf algebra,\nits dual, the Haar state, and the induced Frobenius pairing map.\nThe conclusion (non-degeneracy / bijectivity of the pairing) is\n**not** a field here — it is the named proposition\n`exists_axiom_1_frobenius` below, so the claim is stated, not\nself-assumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}